From 2a8b3d5d5024c048ac1ee999cb876c54b0b1bb63 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: atomozero <bernardi.andrea@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 10:37:37 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 075/203] busses/i2c: add a driver for the embedded controller
 of the Toshiba AC100

The EC ("nvidia,nvec") is the I2C master and talks to a Tegra 2 I2C
controller in slave mode, which we ask to read from us through a GPIO.
Port the transport of Linux' drivers/staging/nvec and publish the
built-in keyboard (PS/2 set 1 scan codes, repeated in software) and the
touchpad (a PS/2 mouse behind the EC) for the input server, and switch
the machine off through it.

It lives in busses/i2c, as drivers for generic device tree nodes are
only looked for there at boot.
